[32m+[m[32m## 6. Kernel-gap diagnostic (TPU v5e-8, KAGGLE_MEDIUM, B=8 L=4096, FP32)[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mRun to test (and rule out) the hypothesis that Pallas-forward's slowness[m
[32m+[m[32mrelative to JAX_REF comes from scheduling/barrier overhead between[m
[32m+[m[32mseparate `pallas_call` graphs, as opposed to the cost of the kernels[m
[32m+[m[32mthemselves.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m**Method:** each forward kernel (A/B/C/D) and each backward kernel[m
[32m+[m[32m(B1-B5) was benchmarked in isolation (own `jax.jit`, real intermediate[m
[32m+[m[32mvalues chained from the previous stage) and the sum was compared against[m
[32m+[m[32mthe full pipeline's measured time. Backward was measured with forward[m
[32m+[m[32mcost explicitly excluded (direct call to `_gdn2_core_bwd` on pre-harvested[m
[32m+[m[32mresiduals, not via `jax.vjp(loss, ...)`).[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m**Results:**[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m| stage | sum(isolated) | full pipeline | gap | gap % | proxy busy % |[m
[32m+[m[32m| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |[m
[32m+[m[32m| fwd | 104.563 ms | 102.023 ms | -2.540 ms | -2.5% | 102.5% |[m
[32m+[m[32m| bwd | 71.995 ms | 72.704 ms | +0.709 ms | +1.0% | 99.0% |[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m**Conclusion:** gap is within measurement noise on both fwd and bwd (in[m
[32m+[m[32mfact slightly negative on fwd, meaning the fused pipeline is marginally[m
[32m+[m[32m*faster* than the sum of its isolated parts, consistent with XLA doing[m
[32m+[m[32msome cross-kernel scheduling even across `pallas_call` boundaries). The[m
[32m+[m[32m"disconnected graphs" hypothesis is **ruled out**. Per-kernel breakdown:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mfwd: Kernel A 47.576 ms <- expensive, VPU pair-sum (see section 1/2)[m
[32m+[m[32mKernel B 51.234 ms <- expensive, MB=16 sub-MXU-tile solve (see section 2/4)[m
[32m+[m[32mKernel C 2.311 ms[m
[32m+[m[32mKernel D 3.442 ms[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mbwd: B2 1.547 ms[m
[32m+[m[32mB1 3.145 ms[m
[32m+[m[32mB3 4.555 ms[m
[32m+[m[32mB4 61.959 ms <- expensive, mirrors Kernel A's VPU pair-sum pattern[m
[32m+[m[32mB5 0.790 ms[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mKernel A and its backward counterpart B4 use the same[m
[32m+[m[32mbroadcast-multiply-reduce pattern (`_weighted_pair_sum` /[m
[32m+[m[32m`_dL_pair_sum`/`_dR_pair_sum`/`_dgc_pair_sum`) instead of a true MXU[m
[32m+[m[32mmatmul; this is the same computation the `use_centering=True` path[m
[32m+[m[32malready factors into real `jnp.dot` calls (section 1). This is currently[m
[32m+[m[32mthe leading, evidence-backed hypothesis for the majority of the[m
[32m+[m[32mfwd/bwd slowdown vs JAX_REF -- not kernel-count/dispatch overhead.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m**Not yet done:** `compiled.cost_analysis()` (flops / bytes-accessed) on[m
[32m+[m[32mKernel A/B in isolation, to directly confirm VPU- vs MXU-bound and rule[m
[32m+[m[32mout simple HBM-bandwidth explanations for Kernel B specifically (its[m
[32m+[m[32mslowness could be sub-tile MXU padding, or could be something else in the[m
[32m+[m[32mrecursive block-solve structure -- not yet isolated from the `use_centering`[m
[32m+[m[32mhypothesis, which only directly explains Kernel A/B4, not Kernel B).[m
[32m+[m[32mxplane/TensorBoard trace visual confirmation was not obtained (no[m
[32m+[m[32mforwarded port in the current environment); the numeric isolated-vs-pipeline[m
[32m+[m[32mmethod above was used as the primary evidence instead and is considered[m
[32m+[m[32msufficient to reject the dispatch-overhead hypothesis.[m
